Modem tables for spesn OS1.0.11.0.TGKEUXM, reading modem_b (0171).

The tables were generated from a spes modem_a. Observed against this phone's backups: 20 of 28 modem
segments differ by CRC and, in the 610-file list, 15 sizes and 259 offsets differ on modem_b. The kernel
checks CRCs, so the old tables could only refuse. Regenerated with tools/map-modem-fat16.py and
tools/gen-spes-modem-tables.py from modem_b, the active slot. This replaces the spes tables: a spes
would now need its own tables back, or fail the CRC check. modem_part= still selects the partition.

